<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines' 11-mo trade deficit at $10.951 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippines' 11-mo trade deficit at $10.951 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines posted a merchandise trade deficit of $10.951 billion in the first eleven months of 1996 against $8.141 billion in the same period in 1995, the National Statistics Office said on Friday.</p>
<p>The trade deficit narrowed to $861 million in November, 1996 from $993 million in the same month in 1995.  </p>
<p>MERCHANDISE TRADE  Jan-Nov 96 Jan-Oct 96 Jan-Nov 95</p>
<p>    Exports		   18.660   16.810     15.826</p>
<p>    Imports		   29.611   26.900     23.967</p>
<p>    Trade balance	  -10.951  -10.090     -8.141</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billion U.S.dollars.</p>
<p>		    ---------</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE     Nov 96   Oct 96     Nov 95</p>
<p>    Exports		    1,850    1,884	1,422</p>
<p>    Imports		    2,711    2,828	2,415</p>
<p>    Trade balance	    -861     -944	 -993</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in millions of U.S. dollars. Components may not add up due to rounding off of figures.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8934</p>
</text>
